{"id":"2e2aaeee2548eb4a","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-09-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.0.0"},"statement":"With Charmcraft 4.0.0 and later, the default `charmcraft init` profile is `kubernetes` (a minimal Kubernetes charm scaffold), the `simple` profile is unavailable, and bundle packing, bundle management commands, and bundle registration are removed; these remain available in Charmcraft 3.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.0/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:25.219935229Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"288f0aaaa46b5391","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-09-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.0.0"},"statement":"In Charmcraft 4.0.0, the machine and Kubernetes `charmcraft init` profiles unite the `static` and `lint` tox environments.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.0/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:43.924535811Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5259c4a9c8b8a0c4","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-09-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.0.0"},"statement":"In Charmcraft 4.0.0, charms generated by the machine and Kubernetes `charmcraft init` profiles are packed with the uv plugin, and their dependencies are managed with uv.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.0/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:43.924535811Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"80a5cc59dc02083a","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-09-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.0.0"},"statement":"The reusable integration tests in the machine and Kubernetes `charmcraft init` profiles use Jubilant.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.0/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:43.924535811Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"905e9896f66f11f8","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-09-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.0.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.0.0 introduced experimental `test-machine` and `test-kubernetes` `charmcraft init` profiles that provide a framework for using the `charmcraft test` command.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.0/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:43.924535811Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"0fcc2831e7806bac","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.1.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.1 adds experimental build support for Ubuntu 25.10 and Ubuntu 26.04 bases.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.1/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:56.496481667Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b2bc09f9e0e42893","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.1.0"},"statement":"The 12-factor app init templates in Charmcraft 4.1 include an optional HTTP proxy relation (`http-proxy` using the `http_proxy` interface, with a limit of 1), and Spring Boot extension profiles support configuring active Spring Boot profiles at runtime; for example, `charmcraft.yaml` can declare `requires:\\n  http-proxy:\\n    interface: http_proxy\\n    optional: true\\n    limit: 1`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.1/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:03.966835265Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8ad0c1cf0fccb11e","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-03-17T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.2.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.2 `charmcraft init` machine, Kubernetes, Django-framework, and Flask-framework templates default to Ubuntu 24.04; the machine and Kubernetes templates assume Juju 3.6 or newer.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.2/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:09.379990789Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"218adf835fe8c5fa","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-03-17T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.2.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft's `uv` plugin compiles bytecode for installed Python files by default from Charmcraft 4.2; set `UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE: 'false'` in a part's `build-environment` to disable compilation, for example `parts:\\n  my-app:\\n    plugin: uv\\n    build-environment:\\n      - UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE: 'false'`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.2/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:13.150640669Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1d90827445fcab15","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-06-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"4.3.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.3 supports packing reactive-plugin charms on Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, automatically enabling the `universe` APT repository for the `python3-venv` package; for example, `charmcraft.yaml` can declare `parts:\\n  charm:\\n    plugin: reactive\\n    source: .`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.3/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:20.724363517Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e4cc66b2df00786f","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-06-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"4.3.0"},"statement":"For charms built on Ubuntu 26.04 or higher, Charmcraft 4.3 rejects part names containing `/`; for example, a valid part declaration is `parts:\\n  my-part:\\n    plugin: dump\\n    source: .`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.3/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:28.897997408Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"9cd08bc1baa79f74","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-06-23T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.3.0"},"statement":"The Django, Flask, FastAPI, Express.js, Go, and Spring Boot 12-factor init templates in Charmcraft 4.3 include commented optional Valkey client relations, and declaring `valkey_client` in a charm's `requires` automatically injects the `dpcharmlibs-interfaces` Python package; the relation exposes `VALKEY_HOSTNAME`, `VALKEY_PORT`, `VALKEY_USERNAME`, and `VALKEY_PASSWORD` to the app. For example, `charmcraft.yaml` can declare `requires:\\n  valkey:\\n    interface: valkey_client\\n    optional: true`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.3/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:37.970597684Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c12cad3e13eeaa46","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-06-24T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.3.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.3's machine and Kubernetes init templates use `pytest-jubilant` for integration tests, include `@pytest.mark.juju_setup` scaffolding, and configure pytest warnings as errors by default; packing a 12-factor charm also validates the structure of a custom COS directory and fails on an invalid layout.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.3/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:46.362489366Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"76ded1e3dc78299e","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-07-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.4.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.4 authenticates to Charmhub using Ubuntu One rather than Candid, with CLI-only login and no browser-based authentication step.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.4/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:53.888062048Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5e4a5581f1ffbe09","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-07-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.4.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.4 supports extension dispatch for 12-factor app extensions, adds base support for Flask and Django extensions, treats warnings as errors in generated tests by default, and validates `paas-config.yaml` inputs; for example, `charmcraft.yaml` can configure an extension using `type: charm\\nbases:\\n  - build-on: [ubuntu@24.04:amd64]\\n    run-on: [ubuntu@24.04:amd64]\\nextensions: [django-framework]`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.4/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:00.569077954Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"94a3b202a97c153c","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-11-03T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.5.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.5 can pack charms in a monorepo when `CHARMCRAFT_EXPERIMENTAL_MONOREPO` is enabled, mounting the enclosing Git repository root in the build instance so charm parts can use shared dependencies in parent or sibling directories.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.5/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:05.371331645Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"275d5776cc8a9f68","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-11-03T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.5.0"},"statement":"In Charmcraft 4.5, `charmcraft init --base` selects base-specific variants for the Django, Flask, FastAPI, Go, ExpressJS, and Spring Boot framework profiles on Ubuntu 24.04 or 26.04; without `--base`, init profiles use Ubuntu 24.04.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.5/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:12.233080765Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7e158bf6f05aebe7","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-11-03T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.5.0"},"statement":"For an extension-based charm targeting Ubuntu 26.04, use the current `base` and `platforms` configuration rather than the deprecated `bases` key; for example, the Charmcraft 4.5 Flask profile template declares `base: ubuntu@26.04`, a `platforms` map, and `extensions: [flask-framework]`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.5/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:12.233080765Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b6343b1b8b959384","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-10-21T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"4.5.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.5 deprecates Charmhub library registration: `charmcraft create-lib` now exits with an error because Charmhub no longer accepts new library registrations, and new or existing charm libraries should be distributed as Python packages.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.5/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:26.229282698Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6e083839b24a2904","subject":"charmcraft","time":"2026-11-03T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"24.04","version":"4.5.0"},"statement":"Charmcraft 4.5 marks the Spring Boot extension for Ubuntu 24.04 LTS as experimental, and the shown charmcraft.yaml bases target Ubuntu 24.04.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmcraft/stable/release-notes/charmcraft-4.5/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:42.832071501Z","by":"agent"}
